# Change records (anti-overlap)

## Every session
1. **Read** `CHANGELOG.md` (and relevant `docs/adr/*`) before planning or editing.
2. Treat locked decisions in the changelog as constraints — do not reverse them without an explicit user ask + new ADR.
3. After meaningful work (feature, architecture, fix, media, tooling), **append** a dated entry under `## [Unreleased]` or a new `## YYYY-MM-DD` section.
4. If `CHANGELOG.md` is missing, create it at the repo root using the standard format below, then continue.

## Entry format (keep short)
```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD
### Short title
- What changed and where (paths / seams)
- Why / constraint to preserve
```

## Do not
- Skip the changelog because “git history is enough”
- Overwrite architecture seams documented in CHANGELOG / ADRs without recording the change
- Dump noisy one-line typo fixes — only meaningful updates
